==============================================================================
COLLAPSE-GATE VALIDATOR (Job 1) -- post-hoc only.  No training, no halting.
==============================================================================
  Agreement = Spearman(DA_ckpt scores, BaselineA_final scores) on the fold's
  UNLABELED target pool.  FLOOR ALARM only -- never maximize agreement (that
  returns the source model).  Firing thresholds are UNCALIBRATED [UNVERIFIED].

==============================================================================
G3 -- SELF-TEST on synthetic agreement curves (known answers)
==============================================================================
  Expectation is stated per case.  A gate that FALSE-FIRES on the healthy
  cases is the worst outcome and must be caught here (spec 5).

  [PASS] healthy decline (gradual 1.00->0.85, then flat)
         expected: must NOT fire
         observed: strict: no-fire(cliff=n,floor=n), loose: no-fire(cliff=n,floor=n)

  [PASS] cliff collapse (0.90 -> 0.20 at step 4200)
         expected: must FIRE at ~4200
         observed: strict: FIRE@4500(cliff=y,floor=y), loose: FIRE@4500(cliff=y,floor=n)

  [PASS] slow slide, no floor (1.00 -> 0.10, never levels)
         expected: must FIRE
         observed: strict: FIRE@5400(cliff=n,floor=y), loose: FIRE@8100(cliff=n,floor=y)

  [PASS] early dip then recovery (dip to 0.72, back to 0.90)
         expected: must NOT fire
         observed: strict: no-fire(cliff=n,floor=n), loose: no-fire(cliff=n,floor=n)

  ALL SELF-TESTS PASS -- the gate separates cliffs/slides from healthy decline and dips.

